   So, you want to know the story of the demon blade Stormbringer, 
   with the power to steal men's souls. Stormbringer and its twin Mournblade, 
   are powerful deamons in the form of swords. The two were claimed by the 
   Elric of Melnibone, and his evil cousin, who's name escapes me, sworn
   enemies.  Elric used his blade make up for the fact the weakness caused by 
   his albinism. In this respect Stormbringer served him well, but the black 
   runesword had a nasty habit of striking down friends as well as foes.

Elric's cousin (and sworn enemy) was Yrkoon (sp?). And not for nothing was
Elric known as a ladykiller by the barbarian tribes with whom he mingled...
If you're planning to read the books, I'd start with "Elric of Melnibone" as
it sets the scene for those which follow.
I *think* the swords were granted to Elric and Yrkoon by the god Arioch, whose
symbol is the sword - the Melniboneans were an ancient race in a world of
barbarians, advanced in sorcery and craftsmanship, who knew the sorcerous
rituals which could be used to speak with the gods: Arioch was Elric's
patron (his battle cry was "Souls for my Lord Arioch!").

Dave (read these a long while ago) Porter

